# Form field density

Match purchase orders. Fields sit next to each other in `FormGrid` / `FormField` from `@/components/ui/form-grid`. Do not stretch every input to a third or half of the card.

- **compact** (default): qty, unit, price, totals, dates, codes, revision, thickness, status, yes/no
- **wide**: remarks, comments, specification, descriptions, locations that need a sentence
- **full**: only when a line must use the whole row

Prefer a single-line `Input` for notes. Use `Textarea` only for real paragraphs, and then `rows={2}`.

```tsx
<FormGrid>
  <FormField><FieldLabel>Qty</FieldLabel><Input type="number" /></FormField>
  <FormField span="wide"><FieldLabel>Remarks</FieldLabel><Input /></FormField>
</FormGrid>
```

Do not use `sm:grid-cols-2` / `lg:grid-cols-3` equal-width grids for mixed short and long values. Keep `gap-3` and `CardContent` at `pt-4`, not `gap-4` / `pt-6` / `space-y-8`.
